  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of time is a complex and multifaceted phenomenon that has been studied by philosophers, scientists, and scholars across various disciplines. While our everyday experience of time is often described in terms of past, present, and future, this triadic structure is not universally applicable. For example, some indigenous cultures perceive time as cyclical rather than linear, with events repeating themselves in a never-ending cycle. This perspective challenges the Western notion of time as a one-way flow from past to future.\n\nIn addition to these cultural variations, our understanding of time is also influenced by our individual experiences and perceptions. A person's sense of time can be affected by their age, health, and emotional state. For instance, children often experience time as passing more slowly than adults do, while people with certain medical conditions may feel that time is speeding up or slowing down.\n\nThe study of time has also led to the development of various theories and models that attempt to explain its nature and function. Some of these theories propose that time is an illusion created by our brains, while others suggest that it is a fundamental aspect of the universe. Despite these differing perspectives, most scholars agree that time is a relative concept that is shaped by our individual and collective experiences.\n\nIn conclusion, the concept of time is a rich and multifaceted topic that continues to be explored and debated by scholars across various disciplines. Its complex nature and cultural variations make it a fascinating subject for study and reflection.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The concept of time is universal and absolute.\", \"Time is perceived differently across cultures.\", \"Our understanding of time is influenced by our individual experiences.\", \"Time is an illusion created by our brains.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Time is perceived differently across cultures.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the passage, which indigenous culture perceives time as cyclical?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The Western culture\", \"Some indigenous cultures\", \"The ancient Greeks\", \"None of the above\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Some indigenous cultures\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What does the passage suggest about a person's sense of time?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It is always affected by their age.\", \"It can be influenced by their individual experiences and perceptions.\", \"It remains constant throughout their life.\", \"It is not affected by their health or emotional state.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It can be influenced by their individual experiences and perceptions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What does the author's tone suggest about the concept of time?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It is a fixed and absolute concept.\", \"It is a complex and multifaceted phenomenon.\", \"It is not worth studying or exploring.\", \"It is only relevant to Western cultures.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It is a complex and multifaceted phenomenon.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What does the passage imply about the nature of time?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It is an illusion created by our brains.\", \"It is a fundamental aspect of the universe.\", \"It is relative and shaped by individual experiences.\", \"It is only relevant to scientific theories.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It is relative and shaped by individual experiences.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
